d parties", "cloud switching Data Act", "OpenTelemetry Collector gateway", "IoT data platform", "fractional CTO Europe", "manufacturing data architecture"], "faq": [["What does the EU Data Act require for connected products?", "For connected products and related services placed on the EU market after 12 September 2026, product data must be designed to be accessible to users, and users can ask for it to be shared with third parties of their choice. Personal data in that data remains subject to the GDPR."], ["Can a manufacturer refuse to share data to protect trade secrets?", "The Data Act allows trade secrets to be protected through agreed measures, and only in limited cases to refuse or suspend sharing. Designing the data model to separate raw product data from proprietary derived models makes this much easier."], ["How does the Data Act affect cloud contracts?", "It includes rules to make switching between data processing services easier, and switching charges, including data egress charges for switching, are prohibited from 12 January 2027."]], "related": ["/fractional-cto-europe/", "/fractional-cto/", "/technical-due-diligence/"], "citations": [{"title": "Regulation (EU) 2023/2854 (Data Act)", "url": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2023/2854/oj", "publisher": "EUR-Lex", "date": "13 Dec 2023"}, {"title": "Data Act", "url": "https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/data-act", "publisher": "European Commission"}, {"title": "Data Act developments: 2026 and beyond", "url": "https://www.mccannfitzgerald.com/knowledge/data-privacy-and-cyber-risk/data-act-developments-2026-and-beyond", "publisher": "McCann FitzGerald", "date": "2026"}, {"title": "Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (General Data Protection Regulation)", "url": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/oj", "publisher": "EUR-Lex"}, {"title": "OpenTelemetry Collector Antipatterns", "url": "https://opentelemetry.io/blog/2024/otel-collector-anti-patterns/", "publisher": "OpenTelemetry blog (Adriana Villel